<div class="about-body">
  <p>What started as a newsletter and video series out of Bravery Media is now a podcast: an ongoing argument against higher ed's habit of chasing whatever's shiny — chatbots, AI search, personalization platforms — instead of fixing what's actually broken. The rule: critic, not skeptic. Test the hype against the data before you believe it, or sell it — and call it slop when a shortcut costs more than it saves.</p>

  <h2>About the Hosts</h2>
  <p><strong>{{ podcast.author }}</strong> leads global growth strategy at Squiz. For nearly two decades he's worked inside and alongside higher ed — running university sites, founding Bravery Media, and building the Hospitable Design framework for websites that serve people and institutions at once.</p>
  <p><strong><a href="https://kibilds.co">Dayana Kibilds</a></strong> is Associate Vice President of Marketing and Community at SimpsonScarborough, an international keynote speaker, and the bestselling co-author of <em>Mailed It!</em>. Her talks, workshops, and weekly newsletter, <em>You Ask, Day Answers</em>, are about turning marketing complexity into plans teams can actually run with.</p>

  <h3>Contact</h3>
  <p>Have a question or want to be a guest on the show? Reach out at <a href="mailto:{{ podcast.contact.email }}">{{ podcast.contact.email }}</a>.</p>
